//! Soundness of the THREE-WAY loop, against `par_reduces_cd_star`.
//!
//! ```text
//! whnf_fuel_red_wh3_par : whnf_fuel_red_wh3 the_red_env fuel e = some r
//!                           -> par_reduces_cd_star the_red_env e r
//! ```
//!
//! # Why the target is `par_reduces_cd_star` and not `whnf_red_step`
//!
//! Because the other option is not available. A three-way step does **not**
//! embed into `whnf_red_step` — not as one step, and not into its transitive
//! closure. That relation's only non-beta congruences are `app_left` and `proj`,
//! so nothing lets a delta or a nested iota fire **inside an argument**, and a
//! recursor's major premise *is* an argument. The pre-pass works exactly there.
//!
//! `wh3_fires_here` settles it by computation rather than by argument: on
//! `cx_stuck` the three-way step fires, while `iota_reduct_stuck_here` records
//! that the plain unbudgeted `iota_reduct` is `none` on the same term. Both are
//! single `Eq.refl` evaluations over the real reflected environment.
//!
//! `par_reduces_cd` has the argument congruence that makes the statement
//! possible. `wh_soundness.rs` reached the same conclusion for the two-way
//! faithful loop and recorded it in its own words: *"not merely unproved, it is
//! unstatable."*
//!
//! # The type that trips people
//!
//! The three-way **step** returns `WhStepR`. The three-way **loop** still
//! returns `OptionType KExpr`. So convoys on a step result are `WhStepR.rec`,
//! while equations about the loop keep `option_some_inj` and
//! `option_none_ne_some_type`.
//!
//! Every two-arm `OptionType.rec` convoy over a step became a **three**-arm
//! `WhStepR.rec`, because the two-way `none` split. Where the old `none` arm
//! consulted iota, `wstuck` inherits that and `wstarved` becomes absurdity;
//! where it derived absurdity, both new arms do.
//!
//! `hiota3` is a **carried, undischarged** residual, exactly as `hiota` is in the
//! two-way leg — discharging it inside the induction would need the loop's own
//! soundness at lower fuel. `iota_reduct_whc3_some_inv` is the raw material for a
//! future discharge.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The three-way par leg, and the witness that forces it.
    pub(super) fn add_wh3_soundness(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_APP_HEAD_WH3_PAR,
            "reduce_app_head_wh3_par: the application-head step reduces PARALLEL-wise, over the three-way loop. Nine head shapes; the lambda head is beta and every other lifts the head's own step. \\
\\
Each of the eight lifting shapes was a two-arm OptionType.rec convoy and is now a THREE-arm WhStepR.rec: the none arm SPLIT. wstuck keeps the iota appeal — opt_app_ilift3 at a stuck head reduces to iota_reduct_whc3, handed to hiota3 — and wstarved becomes pure absurdity, because a starved head propagates outward and the application node cannot then have produced a step. That split is the whole three-way distinction, appearing eight times. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_REDUCE_ONCE_RED_WH3_PAR,
            "reduce_once_red_wh3_par: ONE three-way step is a par_reduces_cd_star reduction. \\
\\
Targeting par_reduces_cd_star rather than whnf_red_step is forced, not stylistic: a three-way step does NOT embed into whnf_red_step at any strength, because that relation's only non-beta congruences are app_left and proj, so nothing lets a delta or a nested iota fire inside an argument — and a recursor's major premise is an argument, which is exactly where the pre-pass works. par_reduces_cd has the argument congruence that makes this statable. wh_soundness.rs reached the same conclusion for the two-way faithful loop and called it unstatable. \\
\\
The const arm is the one piece of genuinely new proof: the three-way step wraps defval_for in opt_step_bind, so the option must be case-split before const_delta_step can be applied — the two-way arm could feed its hypothesis straight in. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WHNF_FUEL_RED_WH3_PAR,
            "whnf_fuel_red_wh3_par: the whole three-way LOOP is a par_reduces_cd_star reduction. Fuel induction: refl where the step is stuck, transitivity where it steps. \\
\\
Note which type is which, because getting it backwards is the trap: the three-way STEP returns WhStepR, but the LOOP still returns OptionType KExpr. So the inner convoy on the step result is a WhStepR.rec while the outer equations about the loop keep option_some_inj and option_none_ne_some_type. The wstarved arm is absurd for that reason — wh_dispatch3 on wstarved IS none, so the loop never claimed a result there, which is exactly the honesty the three-way split bought. \\
\\
hiota3 stays a CARRIED residual, as hiota does in the two-way leg: discharging it inside the induction would need the loop's own soundness at lower fuel. iota_reduct_whc3_some_inv is the raw material for a future discharge. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_WH3_FIRES_HERE,
            "wh3_fires_here: THE NON-EMBEDDING, settled by kernel computation rather than argument. \\
\\
On cx_stuck the three-way step FIRES, returning the real iota reduct at pre-pass budget 2. iota_reduct_stuck_here already records, by the same means, that the plain unbudgeted iota_reduct is none on that very term. Both are single Eq.refl evaluations over the real reflected environment. \\
\\
Together they refute the hypothesis that a three-way step is a whnf_red_step: whnf_red_step's iota arm demands the UNBUDGETED reduct, which does not exist here, and none of its other four arms fits cx_stuck either — beta has no redex at the top, delta cannot unfold Nat.rec, app_left needs a head step there is none of, and proj is the wrong shape. This is why the par leg above targets par_reduces_cd_star. \\
\\
A refutation of a claim about the real environment has to compute over it, exactly as establishing one does. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_wh3_whnf_join()?;
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Joinability of the two whnf results, over the THREE-WAY loop.
    ///
    /// Derived from the ORIGINAL `def_eq_whnf_join` source by exactly two
    /// substitutions, body untouched — the third such derivation in
    /// `join_sources`. That the argument survives unchanged is the point:
    /// confluence does not care which whnf produced the endpoints, only that
    /// both are `par_reduces_cd_star` reducts, which `whnf_fuel_red_wh3_par`
    /// above now supplies. The whole confluence layer therefore transfers to the
    /// three-way algorithm with NO new mathematics.
    fn add_wh3_whnf_join(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        let (_orig, _wh, wh3_src) = super::defeq_whnf_join::join_sources();
        self.add_recursive_def(
            &wh3_src,
            "def_eq_whnf_join_wh3: if a and b are definitionally equal and the THREE-WAY loop \
             reduces both at the same fuel, the two results are joinable. \
             \
             Derived from def_eq_whnf_join by two substitutions — the whnf function and the par \
             leg — with the proof term untouched. Confluence does not care which whnf produced \
             the endpoints, only that both are par_reduces_cd_star reducts, and that is exactly \
             what whnf_fuel_red_wh3_par supplies. So the entire confluence development transfers \
             to the three-way algorithm with no new mathematics; the work was all in the par leg. \
             \
             Carries hiotap3, the three-way iota residual, for the same reason the two-way \
             variant carries hiotap. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

